Mario Kart Wii 3DS Redux: attribution and license scope
=====================================================

This source snapshot continues dudewhat's original Mario Kart Wii 3DS port
and MiniBandit's continuation, with Redux development by epicreds. It does
not carry the original repositories' commit history.

The inherited LICENSE grants MIT terms for MiniBandit's contributions.
The inherited upstream notice states that dudewhat's original release did
not include an explicit license; this snapshot does not expand that grant.
The Redux author has chosen not to declare a separate license for the later
Redux contributions at this time.
Do not interpret the root MIT text as a blanket license for every file.

Bundled and external components
-------------------------------
Kinoko, noclip.website and gclib: MIT; see licenses/.
Citro3D: zlib; see licenses/ and vendor/citro3d/.
ogws and mkw decompilation references: CC0; see licenses/.
CFL Mii rendering source: jamesrhg/cfl-mii, revision and local hashes in
vendor/sources.lock.json; no explicit license was found in the bundled
source or upstream repository root during the 2026-10-25 review.
CFL-tool: separately acquired input, pinned in dependencies.json; its license
terms also require clarification. No tool checkout or IconBody.iqm is shipped.
pycgfx: separately acquired banner converter, pinned in dependencies.json;
no explicit license file was found in the locally inspected pinned checkout.
makerom, bannertool and the SDK are acquired separately under their own terms;
this repository does not automatically download them.

Included artwork and excluded inputs
------------------------------------
Mario Kart Wii and its artwork are copyright Nintendo. The repository
contains eight inherited MK7 marker PNGs and the separately supplied HOME
icon, logo and approved banner audio in tools/release/artwork/. These media
assets are not covered by the MIT license. Inclusion here is not a grant of rights to Nintendo artwork.
Game archives, banner CGFX models, native CFL_Res.dat, saves and compiled
packages are not supplied. Builders must supply the game and system inputs.

This is an unofficial fan project, not affiliated with Nintendo.
The unresolved source-license scopes above must be clarified before claiming
that this snapshot is fully licensed for redistribution.
